The question asks for a single customer, so I'll group orders by customer and take the top one. Ties are not handled; LIMIT 1 returns one arbitrary row among tied customers.

```json
{"sql": "SELECT c.full_name AS customer, COUNT(*) AS orders FROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id GROUP BY c.id, c.full_name ORDER BY orders DESC LIMIT 1", "assumptions": "Counted all orders regardless of status, per the default order count definition; returns one customer even if tied."}
```

